& [Claim]
  + the smallest truthful next experiment is to replace the proven llama harness local reflect boundary with an official MCP child-process call while keeping proof-bearing fixture construction on the host

& [Support]
  + Slice8 already proves exact stateless MCP lifecycle validation
  + Slice10 already proves exact volatile register validate inspect and restart behavior
  + llama_tool_reflection already proves the required tool call tool_call_id result append and second-checkpoint import shape against unmodified llama.cpp
  + exported_artifact_validation_request already deterministically constructs the complete valid request but its cross-crate path imports also compile the entire integration-test module
  + checked-in canonical JSON eliminates that coupling and supplies stable experiment bytes without adding production fixture machinery

& [Counterargument]
  + a reusable fixture library would provide typed construction to every consumer
  + it is rejected for P0 because it either duplicates a large builder creates a core dependency cycle or exposes deterministic signing fixtures as ordinary production API

& [RiskControl]
  + exact digest manifests snapshot tests typed response equality preflight closed schemas bounded records and no-effect tool definitions contain semantic provider and security drift

& [Confidence]
  + high for provider-independent fixture and MCP bridge feasibility
  + high for reusing the existing two-checkpoint transcript seam
  + uncertain for live latency token and call-validity results until the pinned provider is observed running

& [Invalidation]
  + fixture regeneration divergence Slice7 response change Slice8 or Slice10 contract change provider identity change or evidence that the selected projection hides a lifecycle distinction

